ClassiCube for RISC OS
======================

ClassiCube is a free, open source game compatible with Minecraft
Classic: build and explore in single player, or join the community's
servers. https://www.classicube.net

This is a port to RISC OS 5 on ARMv7 (Raspberry Pi 2 and later, and
other Cortex-A boards with VFP). It draws with riscos-mesa's OpenGL
(in software) through SDL 2.

Needs
-----
- RISC OS 5.28 or later (for the AcornSSL module, used for downloads).
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16+ and ARMEABISupport, from PackMan.
- For sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager (ssb.zip from
  https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html), or
  DigitalRenderer.

First run
---------
The launcher offers to download the game's sounds, music and textures
(a few MB). AcornSSL may ask whether to trust a server's certificate;
choose Accept, or Accept always.

Your options, worlds, screenshots and texture packs are kept in
<Choices$Write>.ClassiCube (set ClassiCube$Data before running to
use somewhere else).

Speed
-----
Drawing is done by the CPU. If the game is slow:
- in the game's options, lower the view distance and turn off smooth
  lighting and fancy effects;
- play in a smaller window, or on a Pi take the | off the
  SDL_RISCOS_GL_RENDER_SIZE and SDL_RISCOS_GL_OVERLAY lines in !Run.

Problems
--------
Messages are written to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.ClassiCubeLog (and OpenAL's to
<Wimp$ScrapDir>.ClassiCubeAL).

